    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0151" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg59"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/97: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d83-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-31T21:00:00+03:00">October 31, 1943—9
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1798. For the Acting Secretary from the Secretary.</p>
                <p>At the request of the Ambassador and because of the increase in work here as a
                    result (<hi rendition="#small-caps">DelAm</hi> 47<anchor n="2" xml:id="d83-f2"
                    />) of the Conference, I have decided to leave Bohlen here until the end of
                    year. This would also make him available for the contemplated meeting. I
                    therefore request that the necessary instructions be issued to him for
                    assignment on a temporary basis for two months.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d83-f3"
                    /></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d83-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d83-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the Ambassador, Moscow, in the numerical series of the Embassy’s
                    telegrams to the Department of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f2" n="2" xml:id="d83-f2-content">
                <p>Numeration of messages sent to the Department of State by the American Delegation
                    to the Moscow Conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f3" n="3" xml:id="d83-f3-content">
                <p>On November 3, 1943, Bohlen was designated First Secretary of the Embassy at
                    Moscow, for temporary duty, effective upon the termination of the Moscow
                    Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
